language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Fill a 9x9 grid with digits 1 to 9 so that each row, column and 3x3 block contains every digit once, keeping the given clues.
given input_grid : matrix indexed by [int(1..9), int(1..9)] of int(0..9)
find grid : matrix indexed by [int(1..9), int(1..9)] of int(1..9)

branching on [grid]

such that
$ each row contains every digit once
forAll r : int(1..9) . (allDiff([grid[r,c] | c : int(1..9)])),
$ each column contains every digit once
forAll c : int(1..9) . (allDiff([grid[r,c] | r : int(1..9)])),
$ each 3x3 block contains every digit once
forAll br : int(0..2) . forAll bc : int(0..2) . (allDiff([grid[3*br+i, 3*bc+j] | i : int(1..3), j : int(1..3)])),
$ every filled cell of the input keeps its given digit
forAll r : int(1..9) . forAll c : int(1..9) . ((input_grid[r,c] != 0) -> (grid[r,c] = input_grid[r,c]))
